From: Chad Cormier Roussel <chadcormierroussel@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 16:30:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] airconv: Lower SV_StartVertexLocation and
 SV_StartInstanceLocation.

StartVertexLocation (256) and StartInstanceLocation (257), Shader Model
6.8's vertex shader inputs, were refused. They now read the values the
vertex shader's IDs are already built from: [[base_vertex]] and
[[base_instance]] in a vertex function, and the draw's arguments in a
geometry pipeline's object function. So StartVertexLocation is the draw's
StartVertexLocation, or BaseVertexLocation (negative too) for an indexed
draw. Any other stage still refuses them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/airconv/dxil/dxil_lower.cpp | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/airconv/dxil/dxil_lower.cpp b/src/airconv/dxil/dxil_lower.cpp
index 96a6591..4d12a3c 100644
--- a/src/airconv/dxil/dxil_lower.cpp
+++ b/src/airconv/dxil/dxil_lower.cpp
@@ -674,6 +674,16 @@ Lowering::LowerOther(uint32_t opcode, llvm::CallInst *call) {
   case op::ViewID: // (138): ViewInstancingTier is NOT_SUPPORTED, so the only view is 0
     Replace(call, ir.getInt32(0));
     return llvm::Error::success();
+  case op::StartVertexLocation:     // (256) -> i32: the draw's StartVertexLocation, or BaseVertexLocation when indexed
+  case op::StartInstanceLocation: { // (257) -> i32: its StartInstanceLocation
+    // [[base_vertex]] and [[base_instance]] in a vertex function, the draw's arguments in a geometry pipeline's object
+    // function (dxbc_converter_gs.cpp); no other stage has them.
+    auto v = opcode == op::StartVertexLocation ? res.base_vertex_id : res.base_instance_id;
+    if (!v)
+      return Unsupported(call);
+    Replace(call, Cast(v, call->getType()));
+    return llvm::Error::success();
+  }
   default:
     return Unsupported(call);
   }
